# mbsync (isync) configuration for topo.tw
# Mirrors the IMAP account defined in ~/.muttrc (muttrc.topo)
#
# Usage:
#   mbsync topo        # sync the whole account
#   mbsync -a          # sync every channel in this file
#   mbsync -l topo     # list-only: show which folders would sync
#
# Local maildir lives under ~/.mail/topo
#
# Login note: muttrc's imaps://pham@mail.topo.tw:993 means the LOGIN user is
# "pham" on host mail.topo.tw; "pham@mail.topo.tw" is only the `pass` entry name.

IMAPAccount topo
Host mail.topo.tw
Port 993
User pham
PassCmd "pass mail/pham@mail.topo.tw"
TLSType IMAPS
CertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt

IMAPStore topo-remote
Account topo

MaildirStore topo-local
SubFolders Verbatim
Inbox ~/Maildir/
Path ~/Maildir/

Channel topo
Far :topo-remote:
Near :topo-local:
# Sync every folder except the non-selectable mbox namespace container/tree.
# To skip scratch folders too, append e.g.: !"tmp" !"test" !"imap" !"zl*"
# "tmp" (and cur/new) collide with the Inbox maildir's reserved staging dirs
# because Inbox lives at the maildir root, so they must never sync as folders.
#Patterns * !"mbox" !"mbox/*" !"imap" !"tmp" !"cur" !"new"
Patterns * !"mbox" !"mbox/*"
Create Both
Expunge Both
SyncState *
